<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:theming="clr-namespace:ExpressiveAvalonia.Theming">
  <!-- Source families, pinned commit 77b2199d6f056c2fe829ce25523c34a905e769c1:
       Checkbox.kt (CheckboxImpl, drawCheck, CheckboxDefaults), RadioButton.kt (RadioButtonImpl),
       Switch.kt (SwitchImpl, ThumbNode, SwitchDefaults) and their token objects.
       Source geometry and state:
       1) Checkbox. Current Material specs use an 18-unit container and icon (the pinned
          Compose flag-off implementation uses 20); the outline is a 2-unit
          stroke inside a 2-unit radius. The check is a stroked path with Square caps and join
          Miter through (4,10)-(8,14)-(16,6); the indeterminate mark gravitates every point onto
          the centre line, i.e. (4,10)-(16,10). Theming.MaterialCheckMark paints that path with
          the source path-fraction (checkDrawFraction) and centre-gravitation
          (crossCenterGravitation), including the intermediate state where a check morphs into
          the dash. CheckboxTokens.StateLayerSize is 40.
       2) Radio. IconSize 20 with a 2-unit ring and a 12-unit dot target (the drawn dot radius is
          animatedDotRadius - stroke/2 = 6 - 1 = 5 when selected). The dot radius grows from 0
          through FastSpatial while the shared ring/dot colour follows DefaultEffects; the ring
          itself never animates its size and there is no separate dot opacity fade.
       3) Switch. 52x32 track with a 2-unit outline when unchecked, a 16-unit off handle, 24-unit
          on handle and 28-unit pressed handle. Native OnContent/OffContent count as thumb
          content in the source (ThumbNode.hasContent) and widen the off handle to 24 too;
          MaterialSwitchKnobTrack derives that size from the native content properties, while the
          switch-icons class covers the built-in glyphs. The handle centre stays at 16/36; only
          the diameter changes, so the pressed state snaps
          (SnapSpec) and the release animates. FastSpatial drives both size and offset; the
          32-unit carrier centring already yields the source's pressed inset 2/22.
       4) State layers/ripple. Checkbox rippleColor is Color.Unspecified in this snapshot, so the
          ripple and its hover/focus state layer use the local content colour (OnSurface) at the
          source 0.10 press alpha; radio and switch do the same. Hover, focus and press feedback
          is that shared state layer only: the pinned default colour functions do not recolor the
          box, ring or handle on those states. The theme uses the shared MaterialRipple
          (ButtonInteraction owner), not a second hand-rolled overlay.
       5) Disabled roles come from the component default colour functions, per role: checkbox
          selected container/border OnSurface at 0.38 with the Surface mark undimmed, radio glyph
          OnSurface at 0.38, switch tracks/border/icon/handle at 0.12/0.38 composited over
          Surface. The switch composites are opaque brushes because the source resolves them
          against Surface before drawing; the shared MaterialDisabled* brushes are not used
          because they mix component roles.
       6) Error. Checkbox/radio have no error API in the pinned source. The :error pseudo-class is
          an ExpressiveAvalonia extension that maps the error role onto the same box/outline/mark
          anatomy so DataValidationErrors can drive it; it is declared as an extension, not source.
       7) Focus ring. The source focus indication is a ripple focus ring; this theme keeps the
          existing 3-unit Secondary ring but only under :focus-visible, so pointer focus is clean.
       8) Motion mapping. Source uses MotionScheme springs and per-state specs, which the shared
          MaterialMotion engines execute. Checkbox mark: MaterialCheckMark keeps the previous
          Progress/Gravitation mapping (DefaultSpatial on the way in, snap() for Off ->
          Indeterminate gravitation, and snap(delayMillis = 100) on the way out, i.e. the mark
          holds its last silhouette for 100 ms and then vanishes without a reverse tween). Checkbox
          colours: both box channels and the mark follow colorAnimationSpecForState: FastEffects
          when the target state is Off, DefaultEffects otherwise (Checkbox.kt:633-648,1039-1048);
          the box/border roles snap while disabled, while the mark colour keeps its spring, as in
          the source. Radio: dot radius FastSpatial, shared ring/dot colour DefaultEffects, colour
          snap while disabled, no dot opacity. Switch: thumb size and Canvas.Left offset FastSpatial
          and SnapSpec while pressed (Switch.kt:187-188,301-315); MaterialSwitchKnobTrack reads the
          native drag position as the target and springs the painted offset/size, so drag input is
          not delayed. No finite template transitions remain for these selection properties.
          Reduced motion finishes the shared springs/colour animations immediately; the checkbox's
          100 ms exit delay is a source constant, not a token, so it survives reduced motion.
       Checkbox/Radio minimum interactive size is 48 with the 40 state layer concentric on the
       20-unit glyph. The switch halo is concentric on the handle and overhangs the track by 4,
       as the source component (clipsContent=false) does. Native CheckBox tri-state cycling,
       RadioButton GroupName exclusivity/navigation, ToggleSwitch drag and access keys stay native. -->
  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type CheckBox}" TargetType="CheckBox">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialFontFamily}" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeFontSize}" />
    <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeLetterSpacing}" />
    <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="48" />
    <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="48" />
    <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left" />
    <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="48,*" Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
          <!-- 40-unit state layer inside the 48-unit target; the 18-unit box is centred in both.
               Layout rounding is off for the anatomy group: the glyph centred in the 40-unit halo
               otherwise lands on a half physical pixel at fractional scales and reads as an
               offset halo. Rounding off keeps the source DIP geometry exact. -->
          <Panel Width="40" Height="40" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                 UseLayoutRounding="False">
            <!-- Source ripple (unbounded, radius 20) also draws the hover/focus state layer, so
                 there is no second Border overlay. Press alpha is the source 0.10. -->
            <theming:MaterialRipple Name="Ripple" Width="40" Height="40"
                                    CornerRadius="20" Radius="20" IsBounded="False"
                                    PressOpacity="0.1" IsHitTestVisible="False" />
            <!-- Current Material specs use an 18-unit box and icon. -->
            <Panel Name="Glyph" Width="18" Height="18" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
              <!-- Source drawBox: fill and 2-unit outline use separate animated colours, so the
                   inset fill/border geometry is drawn by MaterialSelectionBox instead of a Border
                   thickness transition. -->
              <theming:MaterialSelectionBox Name="Box" Width="18" Height="18" CornerRadius="2" />
              <!-- Source drawCheck: one path, partially stroked by Progress and morphed into the
                   dash by Gravitation. -->
              <theming:MaterialCheckMark Name="Check" Width="18" Height="18" StrokeThickness="2"
                                         HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                         IsHitTestVisible="False" />
            </Panel>
            <Border Name="FocusRing" Width="44" Height="44" CornerRadius="22" BorderThickness="3"
                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource MaterialSecondaryBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False" />
          </Panel>
          <!-- VerticalAlignment is what centres the label: a stretched presenter would hand the
               AccessText more height than its line box and TextBlock draws text at the top of it. -->
          <ContentPresenter Name="PART_ContentPresenter" Grid.Column="1" Margin="0,8,8,8"
                            Content="{TemplateBinding Content}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                            LineHeight="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeLineHeight}"
                            LetterSpacing="{TemplateBinding LetterSpacing}"
                            HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                            VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                            HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                            VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                            TextWrapping="Wrap"
                            RecognizesAccessKey="True" />
        </Grid>
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>

    <!-- Source box colours carry their own springs (Checkbox.kt colorAnimationSpecForState):
         FastEffects while the target state is Off, DefaultEffects otherwise. -->
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box">
      <Setter Property="BoxColor" Value="Transparent" />
      <Setter Property="BorderColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceVariantColor}" />
      <Setter Property="ColorSpring" Value="EffectsFast" />
    </Style>
    <!-- Source mark: Progress follows checkDrawFraction and Gravitation follows
         crossCenterGravitation. MaterialCheckMark runs the source specs itself: DefaultSpatial
         springs on the way in, snap() for Off -> Indeterminate gravitation, and a 100 ms hold
         followed by a snap on the way out (Checkbox.kt SnapAnimationDelay). Its colour uses the
         same per-state effect spring as the box. -->
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ theming|MaterialCheckMark#Check">
      <!-- CheckboxTokens uncheckedCheckmarkColor is Transparent; the path is empty there. -->
      <Setter Property="StrokeColor" Value="Transparent" />
      <Setter Property="Progress" Value="0" />
      <Setter Property="Gravitation" Value="0" />
      <Setter Property="ColorSpring" Value="EffectsFast" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#FocusRing">
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
    </Style>
    <!-- Source ripple: checkbox passes Color.Unspecified, so the local content colour (OnSurface)
         is used for both the state layer and the wave; there is no press-scale animation in the
         pinned Checkbox. -->
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ theming|MaterialRipple#Ripple">
      <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceBrush}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Selected and indeterminate share the filled 18-unit container with a 2-unit radius;
         their target state is not Off, so their colour spring is DefaultEffects. -->
    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box, ^:indeterminate /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box">
      <Setter Property="BoxColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialPrimaryColor}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialPrimaryColor}" />
      <Setter Property="ColorSpring" Value="EffectsDefault" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ theming|MaterialCheckMark#Check">
      <Setter Property="Progress" Value="1" />
      <Setter Property="Gravitation" Value="0" />
      <Setter Property="StrokeColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnPrimaryColor}" />
      <Setter Property="ColorSpring" Value="EffectsDefault" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:indeterminate /template/ theming|MaterialCheckMark#Check">
      <Setter Property="Progress" Value="1" />
      <Setter Property="Gravitation" Value="1" />
      <Setter Property="StrokeColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnPrimaryColor}" />
      <Setter Property="ColorSpring" Value="EffectsDefault" />
    </Style>
    <!-- Hover/focus/press feedback is the ripple state layer above; the pinned default
         CheckboxColors do not recolor the outline in those states. -->
    <!-- Extension: error mapping. The pinned Checkbox has no error API; the DataValidationErrors
         driven :error class reuses the source anatomy with the Error role. -->
    <Style Selector="^:error:not(:disabled):not(:checked):not(:indeterminate) /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box">
      <Setter Property="BorderColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialErrorColor}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:error:not(:disabled):checked /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box, ^:error:not(:disabled):indeterminate /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box">
      <Setter Property="BoxColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialErrorColor}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialErrorColor}" />
      <Setter Property="ColorSpring" Value="EffectsDefault" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:error:not(:disabled) /template/ theming|MaterialCheckMark#Check">
      <Setter Property="StrokeColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnErrorColor}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:focus-visible /template/ Border#FocusRing"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" /></Style>

    <Style Selector="^:disabled"><Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSelectionDisabledOnSurfaceBrush}" /></Style>
    <!-- Disabled box/border snap: the source uses rememberUpdatedState for these two roles. Both
         resolve to OnSurface at the token 0.38 opacity, so the glyph opacity applies the alpha
         while the two colours keep the source's transparent-fill/outline split. -->
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box">
      <Setter Property="AnimateColors" Value="False" />
      <Setter Property="BoxColor" Value="Transparent" />
      <Setter Property="BorderColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceColor}" />
      <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.38" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled:checked /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box, ^:disabled:indeterminate /template/ theming|MaterialSelectionBox#Box">
      <Setter Property="BoxColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceColor}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceColor}" />
    </Style>
    <!-- The source checkmark colour animates even while disabled (only box/border snap). -->
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ theming|MaterialCheckMark#Check">
      <Setter Property="StrokeColor" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSurfaceColor}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ theming|MaterialRipple#Ripple"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0" /></Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ Border#FocusRing"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" /></Style>
  </ControlTheme>

  <!-- Radio buttons: MaterialRadioGlyph paints the pinned source's single 20-unit glyph (ring
       plus animated dot) from one colour animation, so the dot no longer swaps an ellipse pair
       with an extra opacity fade. -->
  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type RadioButton}" TargetType="RadioButton">
    <Setter Property="theming:MaterialSelection.RadioKeyboardNavigation" Value="True" />
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialFontFamily}" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeFontSize}" />
    <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeLetterSpacing}" />
    <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="48" />
    <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="48" />
    <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left" />
    <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="48,*" Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
          <!-- Layout rounding off, as in the checkbox: the 20-unit glyph centred in the 40-unit halo
               otherwise lands on a half pixel at fractional scales and reads as a shifted glyph. -->
          <Panel Width="40" Height="40" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                 UseLayoutRounding="False">
            <theming:MaterialRipple Name="Ripple" Width="40" Height="40"
                                    CornerRadius="20" Radius="20" IsBounded="False"
                                    PressOpacity="0.1" IsHitTestVisible="False" />
            <!-- RadioButton.kt draws one glyph: a 2-unit ring at radius 10 - stroke/2 and a dot at
                 animatedDotRadius - stroke/2. The source animates only the dot radius; the ring
                 keeps its size. -->
            <Panel Name="Glyph" Width="20" Height="20" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
              <theming:MaterialRadioGlyph Name="RadioGlyph" Width="20" Height="20"
                                          HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                          IsHitTestVisible="False" />
            </Panel>
            <Border Name="FocusRing" Width="44" Height="44" CornerRadius="22" BorderThickness="3"
                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource MaterialSecondaryBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False" />
          </Panel>
          <!-- Same label contract as the checkbox: centre the presenter, not the stretched text. -->
          <ContentPresenter Name="PART_ContentPresenter" Grid.Column="1" Margin="0,8,8,8"
                            Content="{TemplateBinding Content}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                            LineHeight="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeLineHeight}"
                            LetterSpacing="{TemplateBinding LetterSpacing}"
                            HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                            VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                            HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                            VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                            TextWrapping="Wrap"
                            RecognizesAccessKey="True" />
        </Grid>
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>

    <!-- One source colour for ring and dot, animating through DefaultEffects; the dot radius is
         the source's FastSpatial 0 -> 6 and the glyph draws radius - stroke/2. -->
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ theming|MaterialRadioGlyph#RadioGlyph">
      <Setter Property="Color" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceVariantColor}" />
      <Setter Property="DotRadius" Value="0" />
      <Setter Property="ColorSpring" Value="EffectsDefault" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#FocusRing">
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ theming|MaterialRipple#Ripple">
      <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceBrush}" />
    </Style>

    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ theming|MaterialRadioGlyph#RadioGlyph">
      <Setter Property="Color" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialPrimaryColor}" />
      <Setter Property="DotRadius" Value="6" />
    </Style>
    <!-- Hover/focus/press feedback is the ripple state layer above; RadioButtonColors
         only depend on enabled/selected in the pinned source. -->
    <Style Selector="^:focus-visible /template/ Border#FocusRing"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" /></Style>

    <Style Selector="^:disabled"><Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSelectionDisabledOnSurfaceBrush}" /></Style>
    <!-- RadioButton.kt snaps its colour while disabled (rememberUpdatedState) and keeps the ring
         and dot on the single OnSurface 0.38 disabled role. -->
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ theming|MaterialRadioGlyph#RadioGlyph">
      <Setter Property="AnimateColors" Value="False" />
      <Setter Property="Color" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceColor}" />
      <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.38" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ theming|MaterialRipple#Ripple"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0" /></Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ Border#FocusRing"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" /></Style>
  </ControlTheme>

  <!-- Switch: 52x32 track. The handle centre travels 16 -> 36 while its diameter grows
       16 (off) / 24 (on, or off with icons) / 28 (pressed). The 32-unit carrier stays centred on
       Canvas.Left 0 or 20, which is exactly the native drag travel (PART_SwitchKnob.Width);
       MaterialSwitchKnobTrack paints those targets through the source FastSpatial spring. -->
  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ToggleSwitch}" TargetType="ToggleSwitch">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialFontFamily}" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeFontSize}" />
    <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeLetterSpacing}" />
    <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="48" />
    <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="52" />
    <Setter Property="OnContent" Value="{x:Null}" />
    <Setter Property="OffContent" Value="{x:Null}" />
    <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left" />
    <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <DockPanel Name="SwitchRoot" LastChildFill="True" Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
          <!-- Layout rounding off so the 52x32 track, the 40-unit halo and the 16/24/28 handle keep
               the source DIP geometry at fractional scales; otherwise the centred pair snaps to
               different physical pixels (125% gave 24.4 vs 24) and the halo reads off-centre. -->
          <Panel Name="SwitchTrack" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="52" Height="48" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                 UseLayoutRounding="False">
            <!-- The disabled switch roles are resolved against Surface in SwitchTokens and drawn
                 opaquely, so no backdrop layer is needed. -->
            <Border Name="Track" Width="52" Height="32" VerticalAlignment="Center" CornerRadius="16" />
            <!-- Native ToggleSwitch writes Canvas.Left on PART_MovingKnobs for checked state and
                 drag. MaterialSwitchKnobTrack reads that as the target and paints the FastSpatial
                 spring offset (pressed/dragging snap), so no finite Canvas.Left transition is set. -->
            <theming:MaterialSwitchKnobTrack Name="PART_SwitchKnob" Width="20" Height="48" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
              <Grid Name="PART_MovingKnobs" Width="32" Height="48" Background="Transparent">
                <!-- Source ripple is unbounded with radius 20 centred on the handle, so the halo
                     overhangs the track by 4 exactly as the source component (clipsContent=false)
                     does. It also draws the hover/focus state layer; no second overlay. -->
                <theming:MaterialRipple Name="Ripple" Width="40" Height="40"
                                        CornerRadius="20" Radius="20" IsBounded="False"
                                        PressOpacity="0.1" IsHitTestVisible="False" />
                <Border Name="Thumb" Width="16" Height="16" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" CornerRadius="14">
                  <Border Name="ThumbFill" CornerRadius="14">
                    <!-- The 16-unit slot is centred in the handle: a 16-unit handle has no inset,
                         a 24-unit icon-bearing handle gives the source 4-unit inset. -->
                    <Panel Name="IconSlot" Width="16" Height="16">
                      <!-- Native OnContent/OffContent stay available as handle icons. -->
                      <ContentPresenter Name="PART_OffContentPresenter"
                                        Content="{TemplateBinding OffContent}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding OffContentTemplate}"
                                        TextElement.FontSize="16"
                                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center" VerticalContentAlignment="Center">
                        <ContentPresenter.IsVisible>
                          <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static BoolConverters.Or}">
                            <Binding Path="OffContent" RelativeSource="{RelativeSource TemplatedParent}" Converter="{x:Static ObjectConverters.IsNotNull}" />
                            <Binding Path="OffContentTemplate" RelativeSource="{RelativeSource TemplatedParent}" Converter="{x:Static ObjectConverters.IsNotNull}" />
                          </MultiBinding>
                        </ContentPresenter.IsVisible>
                      </ContentPresenter>
                      <ContentPresenter Name="PART_OnContentPresenter"
                                        Content="{TemplateBinding OnContent}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding OnContentTemplate}"
                                        TextElement.FontSize="16"
                                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center" VerticalContentAlignment="Center" />
                      <!-- Source "Icon=True": built-in check / close glyphs in the 16-unit icon slot.
                           MaterialSelection adds the switch-icons class only while OnContent,
                           OffContent and their templates are null, so consumer content wins. -->
                      <Panel Name="ThumbIcons" IsHitTestVisible="False">
                        <Path Name="SwitchOffIcon" Width="9.333" Height="9.333" Stretch="None"
                              Data="M0.933333 9.33333L0 8.4L3.73333 4.66667L0 0.933333L0.933333 0L4.66667 3.73333L8.4 0L9.33333 0.933333L5.6 4.66667L9.33333 8.4L8.4 9.33333L4.66667 5.6L0.933333 9.33333Z"
                              HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        <Path Name="SwitchOnIcon" Width="10.867" Height="8.017" Stretch="None"
                              Data="M3.8 8.01667L0 4.21667L0.95 3.26667L3.8 6.11667L9.91667 0L10.8667 0.95L3.8 8.01667Z"
                              HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                      </Panel>
                    </Panel>
                  </Border>
                </Border>
              </Grid>
            </theming:MaterialSwitchKnobTrack>
            <Border Name="FocusRing" Width="56" Height="36" CornerRadius="18" BorderThickness="3"
                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource MaterialSecondaryBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False" />
          </Panel>
          <!-- Same label contract: the presenter centres itself so the AccessText is exactly one
               line box tall, and a long label wraps instead of being clipped. -->
          <ContentPresenter Name="PART_ContentPresenter" Margin="12,8,0,8"
                            Content="{TemplateBinding Content}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                            LineHeight="{DynamicResource MaterialBodyLargeLineHeight}"
                            LetterSpacing="{TemplateBinding LetterSpacing}"
                            HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                            VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                            HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                            VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                            TextWrapping="Wrap"
                            RecognizesAccessKey="True" />
        </DockPanel>
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>

    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#Track">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSurfaceContainerHighestBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOutlineBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="2" />
    </Style>
    <!-- Thumb diameter is driven by MaterialSwitchKnobTrack (source ThumbNode): FastSpatial while
         released, SnapSpec while pressed or dragging. Only the colours stay in the template. -->
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#Thumb">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSurfaceBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#ThumbFill">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOutlineBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ theming|MaterialRipple#Ripple">
      <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnSurfaceBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OffContentPresenter">
      <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSurfaceContainerHighestBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OnContentPresenter">
      <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnPrimaryContainerBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Panel#ThumbIcons">
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Path#SwitchOffIcon">
      <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSurfaceContainerHighestBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Path#SwitchOnIcon">
      <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnPrimaryContainerBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#FocusRing">
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
    </Style>

    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Border#Track">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialPrimaryBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
      <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="2" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Border#ThumbFill">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialOnPrimaryBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <!-- The off presenter owns a MultiBinding for IsVisible, so the checked state hides it with
         opacity instead of fighting that binding. Both presenters occupy the same 16-unit slot. -->
    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OffContentPresenter"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0" /></Style>
    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OnContentPresenter"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" /></Style>
    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Path#SwitchOffIcon"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" /></Style>
    <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Path#SwitchOnIcon"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" /></Style>
    <!-- Icon-bearing or content-bearing off handle is 24, so the built-in glyph keeps its
         4-unit inset and native OnContent/OffContent does not jump the layout. -->
    <Style Selector="^.switch-icons /template/ Panel#ThumbIcons">
      <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Hover/focus/pressed feedback is the ripple state layer; the pinned SwitchDefaults
         colors only vary with enabled and checked. Source pressed size/offset snap immediately and
         spring back on release; MaterialSwitchKnobTrack owns both, so no pressed style remains. -->
    <Style Selector="^:focus-visible /template/ Border#FocusRing"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" /></Style>

    <!-- RTL: the source lays the switch out from the start edge, so the track moves to the right
         column and the handle origin mirrors. The mirrored Canvas 0/20 positions put the checked
         handle at the RTL start (left); icons/content are counter-mirrored so text stays upright.
         Pointer input is transformed by the same render transform. -->
    <Style Selector="^[FlowDirection=RightToLeft] /template/ Panel#SwitchTrack">
      <Setter Property="DockPanel.Dock" Value="Right" />
      <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Right" />
      <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="scale(-1,1)" />
      <Setter Property="RenderTransformOrigin" Value="50%,50%" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^[FlowDirection=RightToLeft] /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
      <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,8,12,8" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^[FlowDirection=RightToLeft] /template/ Panel#ThumbIcons, ^[FlowDirection=RightToLeft] /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OffContentPresenter, ^[FlowDirection=RightToLeft] /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OnContentPresenter">
      <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="scale(-1,1)" />
      <Setter Property="RenderTransformOrigin" Value="50%,50%" />
    </Style>

    <Style Selector="^:disabled"><Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSelectionDisabledOnSurfaceBrush}" /></Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ Border#Track">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledOffTrackBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledTrackBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="2" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled:checked /template/ Border#Track">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledTrackBrush}" />
      <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
      <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="2" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ Border#ThumbFill">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledOffThumbBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled:checked /template/ Border#ThumbFill">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSurfaceBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OffContentPresenter">
      <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledOffIconBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_OnContentPresenter">
      <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledOnIconBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ Path#SwitchOffIcon">
      <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledOffIconBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ Path#SwitchOnIcon">
      <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource MaterialSwitchDisabledOnIconBrush}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ theming|MaterialRipple#Ripple"><Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0" /></Style>
    <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ Border#FocusRing"><Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" /></Style>
  </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
